# Module Creation Patterns

## Standard Module Template

Use this template for **ALL** new application modules:

```nix
{ config, pkgs, lib, ... }:

with lib;

let
  cfg = config.applications.<app>;
in
{
  options.applications.<app> = {
    enable = mkEnableOption "<App description>";

    dotfiles = {
      enable = mkOption {
        type = types.bool;
        default = cfg.enable;
        description = "Manage <app> dotfiles";
      };
    };
  };

  config = mkIf cfg.enable {
    # Package installation
    environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [
      <app>
    ];

    # System integration (if needed)
    # programs.<app>.enable = true;
    # users.users.alice.shell = pkgs.<app>;

    # Environment variables (if needed)
    # environment.sessionVariables = { ... };

    # Dotfiles management (ONLY if explicitly requested)
    dotfiles = mkIf cfg.dotfiles.enable {
      enable = true;
      modules.<app> = {
        enable = true;
        mappings = {
          # Explicit file mappings here
        };
      };
    };
  };
}
```

## Module Categories & Patterns

### 1. Simple Application Module (fish, git, zed)

**Pattern**: Basic package + optional dotfiles
**Location**: `modules/<app>/default.nix`
**Example**: fish, git, cursor, zed

```nix
# modules/fish/default.nix
config = mkIf cfg.enable {
  environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [ fish ];
  programs.fish.enable = true;
  users.users.alice.shell = pkgs.fish;

  dotfiles.modules.fish = {
    enable = true;
    mappings = {
      config = {
        source = "config.fish";
        target = "$HOME/.config/fish/config.fish";
      };
    };
  };
};
```

### 2. Service Module (adguardhome, unbound)

**Pattern**: System service configuration
**Location**: `modules/<service>/default.nix`
**Example**: adguardhome, unbound

```nix
# modules/adguardhome/default.nix
config = mkIf cfg.enable {
  services.adguardhome = {
    enable = true;
    port = 3010;
    settings = {
      dns = {
        bind_hosts = [ "127.0.0.1" "::1" ];
        port = 53;
        upstream_dns = [ "127.0.0.1:5335" ];
      };
      # ... service configuration
    };
  };
};
```

### 3. Complex Desktop Module (hyprland, waybar)

**Pattern**: Multi-package + hardware integration
**Location**: `modules/desktop-environment/<app>/default.nix`
**Example**: hyprland, waybar

```nix
# modules/desktop-environment/hyprland/default.nix
config = mkIf cfg.enable {
  programs.hyprland = {
    enable = true;
    xwayland.enable = true;
  };

  environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [
    xfce.thunar grim slurp wl-clipboard
    pavucontrol brightnessctl
  ];

  environment.sessionVariables = {
    __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME = "nvidia";
    WLR_NO_HARDWARE_CURSORS = "1";
  };

  security.polkit.enable = true;
  services.greetd.enable = true;

  xdg.portal = {
    enable = true;
    wlr.enable = true;
    extraPortals = [ pkgs.xdg-desktop-portal-gtk ];
  };
};
```

## File Mapping Conventions

### Target Path Patterns

- `$HOME/.config/<app>/` - Standard config location
- `$HOME/.local/share/<app>/` - Data files
- `$HOME/Projects/<context>/.gitconfig` - Project-specific configs
- `/etc/<app>/` - System-wide configs

### Mapping Examples

```nix
mappings = {
  # Single config file
  settings = {
    source = "settings.json";
    target = "$HOME/.config/zed/settings.json";
  };

  # Multiple related files
  config = {
    source = "config";
    target = "$HOME/.config/i3/config";
  };
  status = {
    source = "i3status.conf";
    target = "$HOME/.config/i3status/config";
  };

  # Project-specific configs
  work-git = {
    source = "work.gitconfig";
    target = "$HOME/Projects/Work/.gitconfig";
  };
};
```

## Module Registration

### 1. Add to Applications Registry

```nix
# modules/applications.nix
imports = [
  # ... existing imports
  ./<new-app>
];
```

### 2. Enable in Main Config

```nix
# configuration.nix
applications = {
  # ... existing apps
  <new-app>.enable = true;
};
```

### 3. Optional: Add to Category

```nix
# modules/games/default.nix (if it's a game)
imports = [
  # ... existing games
  ./<new-game>
];
```

## Best Practices

1. **Start Minimal**: Only add package installation initially
2. **Ask for Config**: Don't add dotfiles management unless requested
3. **Follow Conventions**: Use established patterns and naming
4. **Test Thoroughly**: Run read-only validations yourself (e.g. `./script/check.sh`, `nixos-rebuild dry-run --flake .#example` without sudo) and then ask the user to run privileged rebuilds when ready
5. **Document Changes**: Update relevant documentation

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

- Adding configuration files without explicit request
- Creating unnecessary environment variables
- Including "helpful" defaults or themes
- Forgetting to register modules in applications.nix
- Not testing system rebuild after changes
